<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Noáin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1521">1521</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Esquíroz · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-conquest-of-iberian-navarre">Spanish conquest of Iberian Navarre</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Noáin was fought on 30 June 1521 near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pamplona">Pamplona</a>. A Castilian army defeated the Franco-Navarrese force under André de Foix that had briefly recovered Pamplona and most of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-navarre">Navarre</a> for the exiled king Henry II of Albret. The defeat ended the last serious attempt to restore an independent kingdom in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-navarre">Upper Navarre</a>, which remained part of the Spanish monarchy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-noain.jpg" alt="Battle of Noáin" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jorab · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Batallanoain.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
